implementationPlan.description:
Verification gate, run ONCE. Its fresh output is moe.complete_task's verification evidence. Run the executionContract checkRef exactly, from anywhere inside your worktree. It does the following:
- archives the worktree HEAD into a mktemp snapshot outside the repo;
- overlays your 5 owned paths (uncommitted edits included);
- runs `npm ci` under `env -i` with Linux node v24;
- type-checks the package (tsc --noEmit) and the new test file (tt.json, because the package tsconfig excludes tests);
- runs the task's 7 vitest files.

Per the global rail, never run vitest, npm ci or npm test in the shared checkout or in your worktree. A `TMPDIR=<your scratch dir>` prefix on the OUTER command is fine. Never pass TMPDIR into the env -i (mem:convention-daemon-full-suite-gate-checkref: a long temp root breaks tsx IPC pipes).

Expected tail: 'Test Files  7 passed (7)' and 'Tests  112 passed (112)', exit 0. That was dry-run at both 6cca2104 and dc37ea2b in about 10 s with a warm npm cache.

Planning also ran the full daemon suite on the fixed snapshot (238 files, 7061 passed, 24 skipped). The other callers of these tools were green too: attemptHandback, dependencyUnblock, dependencyReadiness.strict, claimNextTask, activityActor, StateManager and chatSystemFeed, 411 passed. No other test asserts 'by unknown' or an absent actor for these four tools, so the narrow gate is the right size for this mid-epic row.

If a file other than taskMoveActor fails, read it before touching anything: the fix only adds an actor.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
updateTask(taskId, updates, event?, actorWorkerId?): an omitted event is recorded as TASK_UPDATED (taskStore.ts:646-650). The #general status line names `actorWorkerId || updated.assignedWorkerId || 'unknown'` (:657). Every move here except the third-party park clears the assignee, which is why it read 'by unknown'. report_blocked has three writes with distinct reachability:
- the flip (:342);
- the already-BLOCKED correction (:359), reached by a re-report with a new reason, or by the assignee acknowledging a third-party hold;
- the grant correction (:144), reached by a re-report on a BLOCKED row whose resourceId is free.
The test reaches each one with its own row. The daemon floors this 4-step, 5-file plan at tier standard (planSizeFloor: light needs <=3 steps and <=2 files).
